---
description: Mobile rules for iOS/Android apps and shared mobile code
version: 1.0.0
globs: ["mobile/**", "ios/**", "android/**", "apps/**/mobile/**", "packages/**/mobile/**", "**/*.swift", "**/*.m", "**/*.mm", "**/*.kt", "**/*.java", "**/*.dart", "**/*.tsx", "**/*.jsx"]
alwaysApply: true
---

- Prioritize UI responsiveness; keep heavy work off the main thread and use backpressure where needed.
- Support offline-first flows where applicable; design clear sync and conflict strategies.
- Manage permissions with user intent; degrade gracefully when denied.
- Securely handle tokens/keys (Keychain/Keystore); avoid storing secrets in bundles or logs.
- Guard telemetry for privacy: filter PII, honor consent/opt-outs, and avoid sensitive payloads in crash reports.
- Detect risky environments (root/jailbreak, debugger) and degrade or block sensitive features.
- Document and test the minimum supported OS/device matrix and revisit quarterly.
- Budget for startup time; lazy-load noncritical features and assets.
- Handle background/foreground transitions safely; save state and release resources.
- Write UI tests for critical flows and integration tests for platform services.
- Monitor crashes and performance (ANR/app hangs) and add breadcrumbs around critical actions.
